hey tasty fam  long time no see  hey guys it's keanu i am here in jaconi  my kitchen studio space and i'm going to  be teaching you today how i make some  incredibly delicious freezer breakfast  burritos plus added bonus my spicy  tomato  jam  super excited to share this recipe with  you guys so let's get started  to kick things off i want to show you  how to make the spicy tomato jam it is  so simple first thing i'm going to do is  chop up my tomatoes playing around with  knives is always fun  in the least creepy way i can ever pose  that  i generally like to make really big  batches of this so i have enough for my  burritos i can smear it on some  sandwiches so put these all in a bowl  try to save every drip of juice and i'm  gonna finely dice onion  get ready for the waterworks horizontal  slices across the onion and now i'm  going to put my knife vertically  and then i'm just going to slice going  as small small small small  as i can  ah  it  hurts so much  after i chop onions i banish them  temporarily from anywhere near my  line of sight  so i can cook in peace  oh  lord have mercy  should never wear mascara while cutting  onions  tomatoes are in onions are in  last chopping really is the chilies  now this is kind of like a choose your  own heat level  situation i like a little tangle so chop  them up super fine  so the final thing i need to cut is just  a lemon it just needs some acid to get  going and i'm just going to slice it in  half  i'm just going to put all the  ingredients inside so  the chilies the tomatoes the onions all  go in and the lemon juice i'm just gonna  squeeze it into my hand using my fingers  to catch  all the seeds so i have a teaspoon of  kosher salt going in if you're using  table salt you'll want to use less  and my spice you'll be using is ground  coriander ground cumin also is a great  substitute so about a teaspoon and a  half of that  and of course some sugar because what is  jam without a little sweetness  i have a cup of dark brown sugar and  then just give it a good mix so i want  to mix it up and you'll even see from  that sugar and like tomato juice  happening together it's kind of creating  a sauce and that's what you'll need  because to cook this is going to boil  now i'm just going to pop this on the  stove over medium heat for about 30 to  40 minutes and every so often give it a  little stir and then before you know it  you'll have some jam  it is burrito time i have my frozen hash  browns and bacon in front of me i'm  gonna cook them on some baking sheets i  have lined with parchment paper for easy  clean up so i'm just gonna cut these  open  spread them as thin as possible  i'm going to hit it with a little bit of  oil i'm using olive oil but you can use  any kind of cooking oil and just some  salt and pepper  you can use tater tots breakfast  potatoes and then on this other baking  sheet i'm just going to put my bacon  slices lay them one by one with no  overlap this works great with any  breakfast meat if you want to make it  veggie friendly on the stove you can  saute some mushrooms with some salt and  pepper  maybe a little bit of white wine in the  end because that  is quite delicious  and both of these are going to go in the  oven until these potatoes are nice and  brown  and this bacon is nice and crispy  bacon and hash browns are in the oven  and the jam is doing its magic on the  stove so time to do the eggs i'm just  going to do simple scrambled eggs i'm  making 10 wraps today so i'm going to  put about eight eggs in there so i just  crack it  on a flat surface  and boom and if you feel like having a  little fun in the kitchen you can try  doing it with one hand  oh gosh i hope this goes well for me  child's play and just whisk  until it is all homogeneous beautiful  yellow  i season them right in here  just salt and then i'm just gonna cook  them in a larger frying pan because  there are so many eggs i'm gonna put in  just a couple tablespoons of unsalted  butter  if you only have salted butter  then do not salt your eggs until the  very end because the butter may do the  job and you don't want to over salt it  so once the butter has these like tiny  foamy little bubbles it is ready for the  eggs i'm just gonna pour them in here  gently scrape the bottom going in  a little figure skater type motion so  a little figure eight here  a little dance around the pan and these  are gonna cook fairly quickly and you'll  see at every time you scrape will come  up in like little ribbons so the eggs  are 90 way the percent there there's  just the smallest amount of liquid left  so that's when i'm actually going to  take it off the heat  eggs are looking perfect it is time to  assemble these burritos  to wrap these breakfast burritos i am  using a flour tortilla now these are  like the little guys they're about seven  inches in diameter if you find your  tortillas are a little stiff what you  can do is microwave them for 10 to 15  seconds  that mobility and flexibility is gonna  help a lot when we're rolling and  wrapping first layer i like to spread on  some  cream cheese definitely less than you  would a bagel  so i go for just like a tablespoon of  cream cheese so i'm gonna go in with  a good spoonful of eggs and just like a  regular eating spoon is perfect to  measure the amount  so just spread that right on top of  where the cream cheese is one slice of  bacon  if you want you can chop it up and  crumble it a few  dollops of tomato jam have to  have to  put so much work into making it don't be  shy  and just a little bit of  that hash brown  nice and crisp  i like putting it on top of the jam  because it helps stick to it you know  and a few sprigs of cilantro so to roll  a burrito i want to make sure all the  fillings are facing horizontally across  and then i'm going to take the two sides  on the left and right and bring them in  and then take the bottom part of the  burrito  bring it all the way up to the top and  then this is where you kind of do like a  tuck and shove  and just squish it all in there  tucking in tucking in make sure those  cilantro leaves stay in and look a teeny  little teeny little burrito and then  seam side down into a hot pan and this  is going to seal it shut it doesn't go  anywhere so once the bottom is sealed  i'm just going to turn it  just to brown all the sides  so give a little crisp just going to  give it a little flip brown the other  side  so these burritos are looking good i'm  going to finish wrapping the rest of the  batch and then i will show you how you  can freeze them  so the burritos are wrapped and toasted  and before i freeze them i have to give  just one a try  oh my god that inside none  honestly feel no obligation to eat this  breakfast all day  lunch dinner midnight snack  i love these  so to wrap these burritos i want to  protect them from freezer burn so before  i toss them into a freezer bag i'm first  gonna wrap them in some plastic wrap pop  a burrito in  wrap it up nice and tight and you want  to make sure your burritos have cooled  down you don't want to wrap a hot  burrito  and then once they're all wrapped you're  going to take just a  big old ziploc bag make sure you write  the date  then you're just gonna pop it in here  fill it nice and tight and chuck it in  the freezer these can freeze for three  months and anytime you want a breakfast  burrito take one out unwrap it and pop  in the microwave and you have breakfast  anytime  if you do make them please show me tag  me on instagram i'd love to see what you  guys are cooking and let me know in the  comments down below what other freezer  friendly meals you'd like to see  until next time  bye oh yes  [Music]

